<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

	<!--
		Wedding collar (2026-09-23). Dragonia's own jewellery, and the item the realm's
		wives wear: a collar a dragon wears with pride, because wearing one means she has
		found a man she judges worth submitting to.

		Worn on the neck, on the Overhead layer, exactly like vanilla's slave collar from
		Ideology - the same body part group, the same layer. It works the other way round,
		though: the slave collar suppresses its wearer, and this one is a wedding gift she
		wants to wear. It is also invisible while worn (see the apparel block below).

		While worn it nullifies the greedy and arrogant traits, hands her the kind and
		masochistic traits, and lifts her mood by 3. The trait swap is the hediff
		(Hediffs_WeddingCollar.xml), the mood is a situational thought
		(Thoughts_WeddingCollar.xml), and the nullifying is the collar's own gene
		(Genes_WeddingCollar.xml): `suppressedTraits` lives on `GeneDef` and nowhere else, and
		it is the only thing that takes a trait out of her list rather than muting it.

		Not makeable and not stuffable: this is bought from Dragonia's jewellers, one
		finished piece, not a thing a colonist tails out of leather. Only the dragonian
		caravan trader carries it, and only one or two at a time - the wiki prices it at
		"as much as a dragoon's first month of pay", which is what MarketValue 850 is.

		Art: Textures/Things/Pawn/Humanlike/Apparel/WeddingCollar/PMM_WeddingCollar.png
		(64x64), used as the item icon - on the ground, in a pawn's inventory, in a stockpile.
		It is deliberately NOT the worn graphic: the collar shows nothing at all on the pawn
		(see the apparel block below).
	-->
	<ThingDef ParentName="ApparelNoQualityBase">
		<defName>PMM_WeddingCollar</defName>
		<label>wedding collar</label>
		<description>A collar of mamono realm silver set with dragon scale and a single magic gem, cut to sit at the base of the throat. Dragonian jewellers in Dragon's Den Alley make them to order, and a dragon wears hers with pride: a wedding collar is proof that she found a man mightier than herself.\n\nThe stone carries the spell. While she wears it, a dragon's pride goes quiet - she is not grasping, and not arrogant - and a gentler woman shows through instead, one who finds a kind of comfort in belonging to someone. Only a husband is meant to fasten one on her, though nothing stops a clever colonist from buying one and seeing what it does.</description>
		<graphicData>
			<texPath>Things/Pawn/Humanlike/Apparel/WeddingCollar/PMM_WeddingCollar</texPath>
			<graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
			<drawSize>0.85</drawSize>
		</graphicData>
		<techLevel>Medieval</techLevel>
		<thingCategories>
			<li>ApparelMisc</li>
		</thingCategories>
		<statBases>
			<MaxHitPoints>60</MaxHitPoints>
			<WorkToMake>3000</WorkToMake>
			<Mass>0.2</Mass>
			<MarketValue>850</MarketValue>
			<StuffEffectMultiplierArmor>0</StuffEffectMultiplierArmor>
			<StuffEffectMultiplierInsulation_Cold>0</StuffEffectMultiplierInsulation_Cold>
			<StuffEffectMultiplierInsulation_Heat>0</StuffEffectMultiplierInsulation_Heat>
			<EquipDelay>2</EquipDelay>
		</statBases>
		<!-- Bought jewelry, not salvage. Without this, the inherited smeltable flag logs
		     "Config error in PMM_WeddingCollar: is smeltable but does not give anything for
		     smelting" on every load. -->
		<smeltable>false</smeltable>
		<apparel>
			<countsAsClothingForNudity>false</countsAsClothingForNudity>
			<bodyPartGroups>
				<li>Neck</li>
			</bodyPartGroups>
			<!-- No <wornGraphicPath>: the collar does not show on the pawn. Verified against the
			     game's own code - Apparel.WornGraphicPath returns this field with no fallback to
			     the item icon, and ApparelGraphicRecordGetter.TryGetGraphicApparel returns false
			     when it is empty, which makes DynamicPawnRenderNodeSetup_Apparel give the
			     apparel no render node at all. Nothing to draw, and no config error.
			     (2026-09-23, on request: she wears it, you just cannot see it.) -->
			<layers>
				<li>Overhead</li>
			</layers>
			<canBeDesiredForIdeo>false</canBeDesiredForIdeo>
			<canBeGeneratedToSatisfyWarmth>false</canBeGeneratedToSatisfyWarmth>
			<canBeGeneratedToSatisfyToxicEnvironmentResistance>false</canBeGeneratedToSatisfyToxicEnvironmentResistance>
		</apparel>
	</ThingDef>

</Defs>
